[[:db/retract 17592186134095 :question/answer-fields 17592186130726] {:db/id 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-656969c6-847a-533c-a9b8-d526f82e1ab3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-656969c6-847a-533c-a9b8-d526f82e1ab3" :question/id #uuid "656969c6-847a-533c-a9b8-d526f82e1ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105694" :question/problem "![](images/17/17637e938a25e91b9a03921dbbe0f22c8ea760f09cfed9b4a76d07bd5e3b9301.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction.\n- $F$ is irrotational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/f3/f385add60afac473a5734f8c1ed57c6575bada03c9c16b24fed73b200c38e2c5.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate clockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (clockwise), our thumb will point into the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points into the screen, in the direction of decreasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a1ff360a-7344-55e5-9541-0cbd28d2ee59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1ff360a-7344-55e5-9541-0cbd28d2ee59" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1ff360a-7344-55e5-9541-0cbd28d2ee59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1524a5a3-8447-5f82-93e3-7232aaf62e6d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-417d24bb-a5fd-5fe7-8f35-35582aaa48b4" "answer-35e57ca5-117c-5fdf-a50f-85738cb2bbce" "answer-1524a5a3-8447-5f82-93e3-7232aaf62e6d" "answer-fb3bf220-d29b-58bf-82fa-15d03e8e1406" "answer-6dd98a2b-6add-530c-b212-292b094d2a67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-417d24bb-a5fd-5fe7-8f35-35582aaa48b4" :answer/id #uuid "417d24bb-a5fd-5fe7-8f35-35582aaa48b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35e57ca5-117c-5fdf-a50f-85738cb2bbce" :answer/id #uuid "35e57ca5-117c-5fdf-a50f-85738cb2bbce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1524a5a3-8447-5f82-93e3-7232aaf62e6d" :answer/id #uuid "1524a5a3-8447-5f82-93e3-7232aaf62e6d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb3bf220-d29b-58bf-82fa-15d03e8e1406" :answer/id #uuid "fb3bf220-d29b-58bf-82fa-15d03e8e1406" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dd98a2b-6add-530c-b212-292b094d2a67" :answer/id #uuid "6dd98a2b-6add-530c-b212-292b094d2a67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133898 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a957b95-e78d-5791-8e30-44fc756d4a5e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134095 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(\\pi ,0).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(\\pi ,0),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(\\pi ,0)} & =-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0)-\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\  & =0-\\pi \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9898eac0-330a-51e3-bb68-1c7f9a46f935"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9898eac0-330a-51e3-bb68-1c7f9a46f935" :answer-field/id #uuid "9898eac0-330a-51e3-bb68-1c7f9a46f935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9a5d28d8-413b-530d-ad6e-efa5df8905f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7113576-7a9c-589a-960b-40c8d014ca07" "answer-9a5d28d8-413b-530d-ad6e-efa5df8905f1" "answer-613b73ad-b4bd-580f-91d8-dabafde0761e" "answer-8cf92fb5-00f1-572a-8207-d72045cf4a6a" "answer-ee35c795-c099-5c49-977b-052171747158"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7113576-7a9c-589a-960b-40c8d014ca07" :answer/id #uuid "f7113576-7a9c-589a-960b-40c8d014ca07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a5d28d8-413b-530d-ad6e-efa5df8905f1" :answer/id #uuid "9a5d28d8-413b-530d-ad6e-efa5df8905f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-613b73ad-b4bd-580f-91d8-dabafde0761e" :answer/id #uuid "613b73ad-b4bd-580f-91d8-dabafde0761e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cf92fb5-00f1-572a-8207-d72045cf4a6a" :answer/id #uuid "8cf92fb5-00f1-572a-8207-d72045cf4a6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee35c795-c099-5c49-977b-052171747158" :answer/id #uuid "ee35c795-c099-5c49-977b-052171747158" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a957b95-e78d-5791-8e30-44fc756d4a5e" :question/id #uuid "5a957b95-e78d-5791-8e30-44fc756d4a5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-131343" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3d405633-3d03-5b83-b9d8-c7d039eaf05b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3d405633-3d03-5b83-b9d8-c7d039eaf05b" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d405633-3d03-5b83-b9d8-c7d039eaf05b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0fd5ff55-9267-592c-8f53-54d27c28ddbe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81f3041d-6679-5b2e-8990-3525e4b2226c" "answer-9811b973-e6d5-574c-9870-5a2db507cfc5" "answer-0fd5ff55-9267-592c-8f53-54d27c28ddbe" "answer-64ee45f8-90e8-584e-9ee0-f763b1794d3a" "answer-d498b33f-c852-5e73-bfc6-bc624cb1045e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81f3041d-6679-5b2e-8990-3525e4b2226c" :answer/id #uuid "81f3041d-6679-5b2e-8990-3525e4b2226c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4xy}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9811b973-e6d5-574c-9870-5a2db507cfc5" :answer/id #uuid "9811b973-e6d5-574c-9870-5a2db507cfc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fd5ff55-9267-592c-8f53-54d27c28ddbe" :answer/id #uuid "0fd5ff55-9267-592c-8f53-54d27c28ddbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64ee45f8-90e8-584e-9ee0-f763b1794d3a" :answer/id #uuid "64ee45f8-90e8-584e-9ee0-f763b1794d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2xy}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d498b33f-c852-5e73-bfc6-bc624cb1045e" :answer/id #uuid "d498b33f-c852-5e73-bfc6-bc624cb1045e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4xy}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e5b5f674-7783-5eb4-b089-af373cffcaf2" :activity/id #uuid "e5b5f674-7783-5eb4-b089-af373cffcaf2" :activity/title "The Curl of a Vector Field" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051085 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-9367b403-efcf-5ce5-86fa-9fe85e17890b" "step-3e935ab0-b71e-5b6d-b820-ffbfd12a9752" "step-b9f70b49-6fa6-5fee-a84d-6cdc4f073bd2" "step-e05e6b0f-4f4c-5280-957e-b076cba38cb7" "step-94cf6f34-eb3b-582a-a36f-1fccec5bf9a0"] :activity/first-step "step-9367b403-efcf-5ce5-86fa-9fe85e17890b" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-9367b403-efcf-5ce5-86fa-9fe8